From b6b0170984cdfa960ac163b3ca167f75f72c4c77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:03:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 33/33] arm64: configs: add omarchy-desktop.config fragment

What an Omarchy desktop needs on J716s beyond the bring-up kernel,
merged after the board and omarchy-usb-host fragments (all =y: the root
has no modules):

- zram swap with zstd (zram-generator otherwise waits 90 s at boot);
- nf_tables + nft_compat + conntrack + the xt matches/targets ufw's rules
  use, for ufw through Arch's iptables-nft (the legacy x_tables, which
  need IP_NF_IPTABLES_LEGACY, are left out); every symbol was checked
  against this tree's Kconfig and verified in the merged .config;
- PWM_APPLE=y (was =m) for the keyboard backlight on fpwm0;
- schedutil as the default cpufreq governor;
- s2idle staging aids (PM_DEBUG/pm_test, PM_SLEEP_DEBUG), hibernation off;
- report-only soft/hard (buddy) lockup and hung-task detectors, so a CPU
  that spins (rather than a whole-SoC freeze) leaves a message on the
  panel. No panic-on-lockup.

The zram and keyboard-backlight items follow edimoldovan/linux-aurora
13c28edbabb6 and 594f4b3a49ec (j714c.config). His firewall list
(00662e9fd517) is not published yet, so the netfilter set is our own,
derived from ufw's before/after rules.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>

---
 arch/arm64/configs/omarchy-desktop.config | 97 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 97 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/configs/omarchy-desktop.config

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/omarchy-desktop.config b/arch/arm64/configs/omarchy-desktop.config
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..180c36c7d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/omarchy-desktop.config
@@ -0,0 +1,97 @@
+# omarchy-desktop.config: what an Omarchy desktop session needs on the
+# J716s (M5 Pro) beyond the bring-up kernel. Merge after the board and
+# omarchy-usb-host fragments. The root has no modules, so everything is =y.
+
+# zram swap: zram-generator otherwise waits 90 s for /dev/zram0 at boot.
+CONFIG_SWAP=y
+CONFIG_BLK_DEV=y
+CONFIG_ZSMALLOC=y
+CONFIG_ZRAM=y
+CONFIG_ZRAM_BACKEND_ZSTD=y
+CONFIG_ZRAM_DEF_COMP_ZSTD=y
+
+# ufw (Omarchy enables it) through Arch's iptables-nft: nf_tables with the
+# xtables compat layer, conntrack, and the matches/targets ufw's rule files use
+# (conntrack/state, limit, recent, multiport, comment, addrtype, hl, pkttype,
+# rt/ipv6header for the IPv6 rules, LOG, REJECT). The legacy x_tables
+# (IP_NF_FILTER etc., IP_NF_IPTABLES_LEGACY) are not needed with iptables-nft.
+CONFIG_NETFILTER=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_ADVANCED=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_INGRESS=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_NETLINK=y
+CONFIG_NF_CONNTRACK=y
+CONFIG_NF_CONNTRACK_MARK=y
+CONFIG_NF_CONNTRACK_FTP=y
+CONFIG_NF_CT_NETLINK=y
+CONFIG_NF_NAT=y
+CONFIG_NF_NAT_FTP=y
+CONFIG_NF_NAT_MASQUERADE=y
+CONFIG_NF_TABLES=y
+CONFIG_NF_TABLES_INET=y
+CONFIG_NF_TABLES_IPV4=y
+CONFIG_NF_TABLES_IPV6=y
+CONFIG_NFT_CT=y
+CONFIG_NFT_LOG=y
+CONFIG_NFT_LIMIT=y
+CONFIG_NFT_MASQ=y
+CONFIG_NFT_NAT=y
+CONFIG_NFT_REJECT=y
+CONFIG_NFT_REJECT_INET=y
+CONFIG_NFT_COMPAT=y
+CONFIG_NFT_FIB_INET=y
+CONFIG_NFT_FIB_IPV4=y
+CONFIG_NFT_FIB_IPV6=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XTABLES=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MARK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_CONNMARK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_LOG=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_MASQUERADE=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_NAT=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_ADDRTYPE=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_COMMENT=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_CONNTRACK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_HL=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_LIMIT=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_MULTIPORT=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_PKTTYPE=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_RECENT=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_STATE=y
+CONFIG_NF_LOG_SYSLOG=y
+CONFIG_NF_REJECT_IPV4=y
+CONFIG_NF_REJECT_IPV6=y
+CONFIG_IP_NF_IPTABLES=y
+CONFIG_IP_NF_TARGET_REJECT=y
+CONFIG_IP6_NF_IPTABLES=y
+CONFIG_IP6_NF_TARGET_REJECT=y
+CONFIG_IP6_NF_MATCH_IPV6HEADER=y
+CONFIG_IP6_NF_MATCH_RT=y
+
+# Keyboard backlight: fpwm0 + pwm-leds (PWM_APPLE was =m).
+CONFIG_PWM=y
+CONFIG_PWM_APPLE=y
+CONFIG_NEW_LEDS=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_CLASS=y
+CONFIG_LEDS_PWM=y
+
+# cpufreq: schedutil by default (validated on J714c with the same OPPs).
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_GOV_SCHEDUTIL=y
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_SCHEDUTIL=y
+
+# s2idle staging: /sys/power/pm_test and sleep debug messages. Hibernation
+# needs the secondaries offlined (spin-table CPUs cannot be) and a resume path
+# the boot chain does not have.
+CONFIG_SUSPEND=y
+CONFIG_PM_SLEEP=y
+CONFIG_PM_DEBUG=y
+CONFIG_PM_ADVANCED_DEBUG=y
+CONFIG_PM_SLEEP_DEBUG=y
+# CONFIG_HIBERNATION is not set
+
+# Hang visibility, report-only (no panic): a CPU spinning with interrupts on
+# or off, or a stuck task, prints a warning on the panel (the buddy hard-lockup
+# detector is the only one available: no perf NMI on Apple). A whole-SoC
+# freeze still prints nothing.
+CONFIG_SOFTLOCKUP_DETECTOR=y
+CONFIG_HARDLOCKUP_DETECTOR=y
+CONFIG_DETECT_HUNG_TASK=y
+CONFIG_DEFAULT_HUNG_TASK_TIMEOUT=120
-- 
